  "rationale": "**Coverage of the `acknowledged_gap` example.** It has one `{test}` reference, at `tests/authoring_cli.rs:235`, on `ollama_cli_delivers_sources_records_fixme_and_keeps_usage_content_free`.\n\n**Scenario setup**\n- The fixture writes `src/lib.rs` with an `{impl}` marker and the comment `// FIXME(#125): one acknowledged gap.` (about line 148). It also writes a `{test}` marker.\n- A mock model server scripts exactly one `submit_judgment` call. It carries `determination: {\"FIXME\":[\"#125\"]}` and the rationale \"src/lib.rs:2 documents the gap.\"\n- The fixture also scripts some earlier tool calls (list, search, read) in the first reply.\n\n**Assertions**\n- The command succeeds.\n- Exactly two model requests are made.\n- The prompt contains the requirement, the definition, and the delivered source (`fn ready()`, `fn ready_test()`). The comment sits in the same delivered file.\n- The saved evidence has `determination == {\"FIXME\":[\"#125\"]}` and the requirement text. Its inputs include the definition and the extra files read.\n- The usage record shows the outcome `completed`, determination `FIXME`, and `evidence_written` true. It also shows the expected request and tool-call counts.\n- The usage record is content-free: it does not contain the `#125` reference, the rationale, or the source text.\n- The stdout summary mentions the evidence and usage.\n\n**Related coverage.** Other tests cover the example's cited requirements. The test at line 548 covers the contrast case, where a FIXME comment sits next to an unacknowledged gap and the model must choose false. `tests/outcomes.rs` and `tests/commands.rs` carry `{test}` references to `requirements.ci.determination` (CI acceptance of FIXME).\n\n**Minor weaknesses.** The test does not assert that the saved evidence inputs contain the FIXME comment line. It also does not assert the rationale text. I found nothing that undermines the scenario, and I found no acknowledged gaps (FIXME) in the test or in the code it exercises. The test does contain the fixture `FIXME(#125)` comment, but that is the scenario's own subject, not an open gap.",
